Obtaining a copy
----------------

IEEE 2030.5 is available at no charge through the IEEE GET Program:

    https://standards.ieee.org/products-programs/ieee-get-program/

Accept IEEE's terms and download the standard. The normative schema is
distributed with the standard's XML artifacts (the XML/xmlspy model release),
where it appears as sep.xsd. Your use of that file is governed by IEEE's
terms, not by this project's license.

This module gates against one specific document: IEEE 2030.5-2018, Model
Build 20180301, sep.xsd. See schema/PROVENANCE.md for its identity, the
digest the tests verify, and how to check a copy you have obtained.


Pointing the build at your copy
-------------------------------

Either place the file at the conventional location, which is gitignored so it
cannot be committed by accident:

    schema/sep.xsd

or set an environment variable to any path you like:

    export SEP2_SCHEMA_PATH=/path/to/sep.xsd

SEP2_SCHEMA_PATH wins over the conventional location. Then:

    go test ./...

Without a copy, the schema-gated tests SKIP and the rest of the suite runs
normally, so a contributor who has not obtained the standard still gets a
green build. The skip is reported by go test as a skip, never as a pass, and
each skipped test names SEP2_SCHEMA_PATH and this file.

A skip is not a validation. To require that a schema really was found, so
that a missing or misconfigured copy fails the run instead of quietly
skipping the gate, set:

    export SEP2_SCHEMA_REQUIRED=1

Continuous integration that supplies the schema should set it. With it set,
an absent schema is a hard failure; the value must be a boolean that Go's
strconv.ParseBool accepts, and anything else is itself an error, so a typo
cannot silently disarm the gate.


The Go Programming Language (pkg/sep2tls/gotls)
------------------------------------------------

pkg/sep2tls/gotls is a fork of the Go standard library's crypto/tls package,
carrying the mandatory IEEE 2030.5 CCM-8 cipher suite that upstream does not
implement. See pkg/sep2tls/gotls/UPSTREAM.md for the exact upstream release,
commit, and the list of deliberate changes.

